  "content": {
    "id": "p14-q4-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "Find $x\\in[0,2\\pi]$ for which:",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p14-q4-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\cos^2x=2\\cos x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\dfrac{\\pi}{2},\\dfrac{3\\pi}{2}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\cos^2x-2\\cos x&=0\\\\\\cos x(\\cos x-2)&=0\\end{align*}$$\nThus $\\cos x=0$ or $\\cos x=2$. Since $-1\\le\\cos x\\le1$, reject $\\cos x=2$.\n$$x=\\frac{\\pi}{2},\\frac{3\\pi}{2}.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q4-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\sin x=\\cos x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\dfrac{\\pi}{4},\\dfrac{5\\pi}{4}$.",
          "worked": "When $\\cos x=0$, $\\sin x=\\pm1$, so these values do not satisfy the equation. Hence divide by $\\cos x$:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}&=1\\\\\\tan x&=1\\end{align*}$$\nThe reference angle is $\\frac{\\pi}{4}$, and tangent is positive in Quadrants I and III.\n$$x=\\frac{\\pi}{4},\\frac{5\\pi}{4}.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q4-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$2\\sin^2x=\\sin x+1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\dfrac{\\pi}{2},\\dfrac{7\\pi}{6},\\dfrac{11\\pi}{6}$.\n\nFactorise the quadratic in $\\sin x$.",
          "worked": "Let $a=\\sin x$.\n$$\\begin{align*}2a^2&=a+1\\\\2a^2-a-1&=0\\\\(2a+1)(a-1)&=0\\end{align*}$$\nThus $\\sin x=-\\tfrac12$ or $\\sin x=1$. For $\\sin x=-\\tfrac12$, the reference angle is $\\frac{\\pi}{6}$ and sine is negative in Quadrants III and IV. For $\\sin x=1$, $x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}$.\n$$x=\\frac{\\pi}{2},\\frac{7\\pi}{6},\\frac{11\\pi}{6}.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 43
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q4-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\sin x=2\\cos^2x+1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}$.\n\nUse $\\cos^2x=1-\\sin^2x$ and factorise.",
          "worked": "Use $\\cos^2x=1-\\sin^2x$ and let $a=\\sin x$.\n$$\\begin{align*}a&=2(1-a^2)+1\\\\2a^2+a-3&=0\\\\(2a+3)(a-1)&=0\\end{align*}$$\nThus $\\sin x=-\\tfrac32$ or $\\sin x=1$. Reject $-\\tfrac32$ because sine lies between $-1$ and $1$.\n$$x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 45
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q4-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$\\sin x+\\csc x=\\dfrac52$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\dfrac{\\pi}{6},\\dfrac{5\\pi}{6}$.\n\nReplace $\\csc x$ by $\\frac{1}{\\sin x}$ and factorise the resulting quadratic.",
          "worked": "Since $\\csc x$ is defined, $\\sin x\\ne0$. Let $a=\\sin x$.\n$$\\begin{align*}a+\\frac1a&=\\frac52\\\\2a^2+2&=5a\\\\2a^2-5a+2&=0\\\\(2a-1)(a-2)&=0\\end{align*}$$\nThus $\\sin x=\\tfrac12$ or $\\sin x=2$. Reject $2$. The reference angle is $\\frac{\\pi}{6}$, and sine is positive in Quadrants I and II.\n$$x=\\frac{\\pi}{6},\\frac{5\\pi}{6}.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q4-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$\\sin x+2\\cos x-2\\sin x\\cos x=1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\dfrac{\\pi}{3},\\dfrac{\\pi}{2},\\dfrac{5\\pi}{3}$.\n\nFactorise by grouping to obtain $(\\sin x-1)(1-2\\cos x)=0$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\sin x+2\\cos x-2\\sin x\\cos x-1&=0\\\\(\\sin x-1)-2\\cos x(\\sin x-1)&=0\\\\(\\sin x-1)(1-2\\cos x)&=0\\end{align*}$$\nThus $\\sin x=1$ or $\\cos x=\\tfrac12$. Sine equals $1$ at $\\frac{\\pi}{2}$; cosine equals $\\tfrac12$ in Quadrants I and IV with reference angle $\\frac{\\pi}{3}$.\n$$x=\\frac{\\pi}{3},\\frac{\\pi}{2},\\frac{5\\pi}{3}.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      }
    ]
  },
